WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.720
Please welcome Kelly Marie Tran.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.461
(audience applauding)

3
00:00:06.461 --> 00:00:07.610
Hello.

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.443
Hi.

5
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.560
Oh my gosh, I am such a fan of you.

6
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.390
I'm so excited to be talking to you (laughs).

7
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:18.163
Oh, my daughters and I are freaking out that you're here.

8
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.280
And there was so many things

9
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.290
I couldn't wait to discuss with you.

10
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:29.780
I loved how you talked about that Raya is a warrior

11
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.810
and not just a princess.

12
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.900
And I did a film called "Ever After"

13
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.040
that was like a spin on "Cinderella"

14
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.620
because we need to be told not to wait to be rescued,

15
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.040
but to rescue ourselves and maybe even others

16
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.500
while we're at it.

17
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.500
So, what spoke to you about getting to be Disney's new

18
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.330
first Southeast Asian warrior princess?

19
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.230
I'm just so excited to be part of the movie.

20
00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.350
Like you said, that sort of broadening the narrative

21
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.290
when it comes to what do people think

22
00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.960
when they think of the word princess?

23
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.320
What do people think when they think of the word hero?

24
00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.600
And recognizing that

25
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.620
I think you've had a very narrow perception

26
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.260
of what those words mean.

27
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.820
And now to be sort of part of that change

28
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.790
and recognizing that Raya, like you said,

29
00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.230
is a character who very much saves herself

30
00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.820
and also is working to save a lot other people around her.

31
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.930
I think that is really important

32
00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.580
and it's really cool to be a part of.

33
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.000
I also know that you are the first Asian woman

34
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.220
to be in these "Star Wars" movies.

35
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.290
Talk about history, we all grew up on "Star Wars"

36
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.080
and you're the first?

37
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.610
I suppose it should have been earlier,

38
00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.440
but thank you for being the first.

39
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.700 line:15%
Gosh, "Star Wars" is such like a big thing

40
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.950 line:15%
for so many people, and to have been a part of that

41
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.100 line:15%
really meant a lot to me.

42
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.660 line:15%
And I think we've talked a lot about what it means

43
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.570 line:15%
to be the first fill in the blank all the time.

44
00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.110
And I think for me, it's really exciting to be part of,

45
00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.690
but also recognizing that I hope that I'm not the last

46
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.380
to be able to do this.

47
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.370
You are also a first on the cover of "Vanity Fair"

48
00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:06.203
for "Star Wars".

49
00:02:06.203 --> 00:02:10.090
You are breaking so many important glass ceilings

50
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.760
and paving the way for others.

51
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.760
And I understand that "Mulan" Disney's first Asian princess,

52
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.960
also a staple in my household.

53
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.190
I've seen it a billion times and we love it.

54
00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.190
That that was something that was an inspiration to you.

55
00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.070
Yeah, that was such a huge part of my childhood.

56
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.330
I think I was nine when that movie came out

57
00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.340
and it was the first time I felt like I saw someone

58
00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.950
who looked like me living in these sort of spaces

59
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.060
on that sort of scale.

60
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.820
And Ming-Na Wen who plays Mulan

61
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.590
is such an inspiration to me.

62
00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.130
And I actually got to meet her at the episode nine premier.

63
00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:55.240
And she's such a symbol of all the things that I wanna be.

64
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.390
It's such a cool experience.

65
00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.278
Well, Ming-Na are you there?

66
00:03:00.278 --> 00:03:01.350
(Kelly gasps)

67
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.840
Hello?

68
00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.191
Oh my God, what?

69
00:03:04.191 --> 00:03:05.831
(all laugh)

70
00:03:05.831 --> 00:03:07.248
Kelly, hi Drew.

71
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.199
Hi, Ming-Na.
Hello everyone.

72
00:03:10.199 --> 00:03:12.805
(audience applauding)

73
00:03:12.805 --> 00:03:15.111
Hi beautiful princess warrior.

74
00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:18.930
Wow, you did not tell me this was happening.

75
00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.159
I'm probably gonna cry a little bit.

76
00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.988
Hi, how are you.

77
00:03:22.988 --> 00:03:24.840
Oh, look at you.

78
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.323
Oh my gosh, how are you doing?

79
00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.510
I'm doing great.

80
00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.510
Congratulations on everything.

81
00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.320
I feel like I'm looking in a mirror,

82
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:38.010
like at the younger, because I followed Kelly's footsteps

83
00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.350
and became part of the Star Wars family.

84
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.320
And now she's followed my footsteps

85
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.710
in being a Disney princess.

86
00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:49.090
I just feel like we have this whole mirror thing going on

87
00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.454
and I love it.
I know.

88
00:03:50.454 --> 00:03:53.880
And I'm so proud of you.

89
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:57.650
And I'm also geek, so you're going to have to sign my doll.

90
00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.643
Yeah!
Okay?

91
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.010
I love that.

92
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.880
These are collectibles for a reason,

93
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.520
because they are symbols.

94
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.330
I mean, we're talking about Disney princesses

95
00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.010
you are Mulan and Raya.

96
00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:16.010
These are the faces, the embodiments, the voices

97
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.530
and the realization of people seeing themselves in you both.

98
00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:27.140
And Kelly, I know that you actually got off social media

99
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.450
because you were having a hard time during "Star Wars",

100
00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.433
because people felt in the cyber world,

101
00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.720
entitled and enabled to say things that were not kind.

102
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.580
I would love to ask you guys

103
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:46.580
in the face of what everybody is going through right now

104
00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.520
in the Asian community,

105
00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.680
do you have any advice out there for any girl, woman

106
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.370
or any age in between who might be watching this,

107
00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.310
of how to find their superhero strength

108
00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.233
in this time right now?

109
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:06.750
I think what Drew was asking about the anti-Asian hate

110
00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:10.753
that's out there.

111
00:05:10.753 --> 00:05:13.670
I mean the anti-Asian hate out there is...

112
00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.770
I have a daughter who's 20

113
00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.310
and she's going to college in New York.

114
00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.630
And as a mother, is a great fear.

115
00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.563
It's a constant fear.

116
00:05:25.986 --> 00:05:28.320 line:15%
And it kinda boggles my mind a little bit

117
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.783 line:15%
that it's happening still.

118
00:05:32.287 --> 00:05:35.630 line:15%
So, I really hope your film "Raya",

119
00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.610
as "Mulan" has done, it crosses all barriers.

120
00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:43.610
It's about finding the hero and the heroine in all of us.

121
00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.410
It's about believing in yourself.

122
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.300
And it's also about having compassion

123
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.300
and sharing the love to fight for humanity

124
00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.420
and fight for what's right?

125
00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.437
So, you know all those messages is really, really important.

126
00:06:01.437 --> 00:06:03.070
And I think "Raya" is gonna provide that

127
00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.940
for the new generation.

128
00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.720
And I'm very grateful for that.

129
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.030
And thank you Drew for asking that question.

130
00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.580
It's a very serious question.

131
00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.220
And I'm just also geeking out a little bit about you Drew.

132
00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.700
Oh my gosh!

133
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.910
You have given us so much.

134
00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:20.070 line:15%
I mean, seriously, your career.

135
00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:24.840 line:15%
Talk about storytelling and offering so much joy

136
00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.943 line:15%
and entertainment as well as,

137
00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.820
just you know, you're my idol.

138
00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.250
Thank you.
You're amazing.

139
00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.060
That moves me so much.
We love you Drew!

140
00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:40.060
I just want all girls to believe that we are equal

141
00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.080
and that we have all the strengths

142
00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.380
and capabilities and possibilities.

143
00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.210
So, I honor the women who prove that narrative to be true

144
00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.150
such as yourselves.

145
00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.610
So, thank you so much for being here today.

146
00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.648
Thank you.

147
00:06:57.648 --> 00:06:58.481
(audience applauding)

148
00:06:58.481 --> 00:07:00.145
All right, air hug.

149
00:07:00.145 --> 00:07:01.400
(audience applauding)

150
00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.280
Also in honor of bravery and resilience

151
00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.600
that you guys have shown and everyone,

152
00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:09.710
we wanna also just contribute $5,000

153
00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:13.320
to the Stop AAPI Hate organization,

154
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:16.610 line:15%
an incredible organization that promotes equality

155
00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.720 line:15%
and provides resources for the Asian American

156
00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.060 line:15%
and Pacific Islander community.

157
00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:26.180 line:15%
And that is just a humble thank you

158
00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:29.610
towards an organization that is doing incredible things.

159
00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:33.570
Ming-Na Wen and Kelly Marie Tran, "Mulan"

160
00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:38.570
and "Raya The Last Dragon" is in theaters and on Disney+

161
00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.350
with premier access on March 5th.

162
00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.350
It's incredible, we loved it.

163
00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.984 line:15%
And we love both of you.

164
00:07:45.984 --> 00:07:48.567 line:15%
(upbeat music)

